import json
from pathlib import Path
facts=['Atomicity makes a transaction an all-or-nothing operation.','Consistency preserves database rules before and after a transaction.','Isolation prevents concurrent transactions from observing intermediate changes.','Durability preserves committed changes after a restart.','A primary key uniquely identifies a row in a table.','A foreign key references a key in another table.']
extra=['An index can speed up reads but adds maintenance work to writes.','A rollback discards the changes of an uncommitted transaction.','A deadlock occurs when transactions wait on one another in a cycle.','Normalization reduces redundant storage of facts.','A backup is a separate copy used for recovery.','A transaction log records changes used during recovery.']
long_notes=['Atomicity makes a transaction an all-or-nothing operation, so a transfer that subtracts money from one account and adds it to another must complete both changes or neither change.', 'Consistency preserves database rules before and after a transaction, meaning a transaction that begins with valid data must end with data that still satisfies the defined constraints.', 'Isolation prevents concurrent transactions from observing intermediate changes, allowing the system to control interactions between operations that overlap in time rather than treating their unfinished values as final.', 'Durability preserves committed changes after a restart, so once the database reports that a transaction has committed, a later restart should not erase that committed result.', 'A primary key uniquely identifies a row in a table, giving each stored record an identifier that can distinguish it from every other row in the same table.', 'A foreign key references a key in another table, connecting related records and supporting a constraint that the referenced identifier must exist when the relationship requires it.', 'An index can speed up reads but adds maintenance work to writes, because changing indexed data may also require changing the supporting structure used to locate those records.', 'A rollback discards the changes of an uncommitted transaction, restoring the transaction state so that partial work does not remain as though the entire operation had succeeded.', 'A deadlock occurs when transactions wait on one another in a cycle, leaving each participant unable to proceed until the database or application breaks that waiting relationship.', 'Normalization reduces redundant storage of facts, organizing related attributes into tables so that updating a fact does not require maintaining unnecessary copies across multiple stored records.', 'A backup is a separate copy used for recovery, providing stored information that can help restore a database when the active copy is damaged or otherwise unavailable.', 'A transaction log records changes used during recovery, allowing the recovery process to identify recorded operations and restore the appropriate state after an interruption affects normal database operation.']
